---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "When Not to Refinance (Red flags)";
const description =
  "Scenarios where refinancing often does not make sense and how to spot red flags. Educational use only.";
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/guides/refinance-when-not-to-refinance">
  <section class="card hero">
    <span class="pill">Guide</span>
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/guides">Guides</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span aria-current="page">When not to refi</span>
    </nav>
    <h1>When not to refinance</h1>
    <p>
      Refinancing is not always beneficial. This guide highlights red flags that usually make a refinance unattractive, even when the
      rate looks lower.
    </p>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/guides/refinance-break-even">Refinance break-even</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/refinance-checklist">Refinance checklist</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/topics/refinance">Refinance topic hub</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Common red flags</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Break-even timeline is longer than your expected time in the home.</li>
      <li>Term resets to 30 years and increases total interest.</li>
      <li>Fees are high relative to monthly savings.</li>
      <li>You plan to move or refinance again within a short period.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Short horizon warning</h2>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0">
      If you may move in 12-24 months, a refinance usually does not recover costs unless there is a lender credit or a large rate
      drop.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Term reset warning</h2>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0">
      A lower rate can still increase total interest if you extend the term. Compare remaining interest on your current loan to the
      new loan interest over your horizon.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Decision checklist</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Break-even date vs expected move or refinance window.</li>
      <li>New loan term compared to remaining term.</li>
      <li>Cash-to-close impact on emergency reserves.</li>
      <li>Rate savings after fees and points.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Decision inputs</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>How long you expect to keep the home.</li>
      <li>Monthly payment relief you actually need.</li>
      <li>Whether you can shorten the term instead.</li>
      <li>Closing costs as a percentage of balance.</li>
      <li>Opportunity cost of using cash to close.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">FAQ</h2>
    <h3 style="margin:12px 0 0">What if I need the lower payment?</h3>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:8px 0 0">
      A lower payment can help cash flow, but compare the long-term cost. Consider short-term alternatives like recasting or extra
      principal payments.
    </p>
    <h3 style="margin:12px 0 0">Is a small rate drop enough?</h3>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:8px 0 0">
      Not always. If costs are high, a small rate drop may take many years to break even.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="grid" style="margin-top:18px">
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Related tools</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li><a href="/calculators/mortgage-payment-calculator">Mortgage payment calculator</a></li>
        <li><a href="/calculators/amortization-schedule-calculator">Amortization schedule</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Related guides</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li><a href="/guides/refinance-break-even">Refinance break-even</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/refinance-rate-vs-term-tradeoff">Rate vs term tradeoff</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/refinance-reset-amortization">Reset amortization</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Next steps</h2>
    <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top:10px">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/guides/refinance-break-even">Break-even guide</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/topics/refinance">Refinance topic hub</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/refinance-checklist">Refinance checklist</a>
    </div>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0">Educational use only. Not financial advice.</p>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0; font-size:13px">Last updated: 2026-01-31</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
